{"Title":"An Act relative to accurate impairment testing","BillNumber":"H3414","DocketNumber":"HD1565","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"DMR1","Name":"David M. Rogers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DMR1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:26:02.36"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"DMR1","Name":"David M. Rogers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DMR1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T15:26:02.36"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3414/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Rogers of Cambridge, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3414) of David M. Rogers relative to testing for operating a motor vehicle while under the influence.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  Section 24 (4)(f)(1) of Chapter 90 is hereby amended by inserting the following after the word “decision”:-\r\n\tNo driver shall have their driver’s license suspended or be otherwise sanctioned for refusing a test that has not been scientifically proven to indicate a level of personal impairment resulting in inability to safely operate a motor vehicle.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}